<title>NETHERLANDS: Van Lanschot cuts Oce to outperformer.</title>
<headline>Van Lanschot cuts Oce to outperformer.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of March 6 research.</p>
<p>Company--------------Sector----------Price----Broker-------</p>
<p>Oce van der Grinten  Office equipm.  238.00  Van Lanschot</p>
<p>COMMENT: OUTPERFORMER (Strong Outperformer). The downgrade of Oce to outperformer is purely because of Oce's impressive share price performance (92 pct in 1996 and 27 pct in 1997 to date). Prospects for earnings growth remain good. Looking at the geographical spread, it is striking that 27 pct of total sales is dirived from the depressed markets Germany and France. When these markets recover they are likely to give Oce new impetus.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS	P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     9.06     26.3   9.6    3.00</p>
<p>    1997		 10.80     22.1   8.2    3.50</p>
<p>    1998		 12.60     18.9   7.4    4.00</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
